      "title": "Research Associate I",
      "description": "Research Associate I - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Research Associate I Martin, TN, United States Trending Job Description The Research Associate I will work under the supervision of the Director of Institutional Research and will collect data for the support of institutional effectiveness, planning, and assessment at the University of Tennessee at Martin.  Various data is needed both to fulfill required external reports and to support strategic planning and decision-making at the university level.  The position assists with all aspects of institutional research and collaborates with others to develop and deliver effective data products.  Subject to change, this position will consist of one day of remote work, with the remainder of the week on site. Responsibilities Work within Institutional Research to fulfill university information needs, including identifying the information needed in reports/data visualizations, retrieving data from relevant sources, and developing the final products/visualizations needed to deliver complete reporting solutions. Perform systematic extraction, analysis, and reporting of quantitative and qualitative university data for state/national reports and surveys. Extract and analyze data for ad-hoc reports pertaining to students, faculty, staff, and instructional processes. Qualifications Minimum Requirements Bachelor degree. Candidate must have at least 1 year of experience with analyzing and reporting data, either in the workplace or in an academic setting. This experience must also include working with Microsoft Excel and other Office products to analyze and report data. Preferred Requirements SQL programming Reporting tools such as SAS, Argos, SAS Visual Analytics, Power BI, etc. Statistical analysis software such as SAS, R, Python, etc Application Process: Applicants must apply online and submit a cover letter, resume, and three references Application Deadline: Applicant review will begin immediately and continue until a candidate has been identified Minimum hiring rate $50,185.38 (Market Range 10) - Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 9524 Job Category Data Analytics Posting Date 08/13/2026, 12:01 PM Job Schedule Full time Locations 554 University Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US EEO/AA STATEMENT / NON-DISCRIMINATION STATEMENT The University of Tennessee is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA institution in the provision of its education and employment programs and services. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of, race, color, national origin, religion, sex, pregnancy, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, or covered veteran status. Inquiries and charges of violation of Title VI (race, color, national origin), Title IX (sex), Section 504 (disability), ADA (disability), ADEA (age), sexual orientation, or veteran status should be directed to the (EEO). Requests for accommodation of a disability should be directed to the ADA Coordinator at the EEO office . © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 554 University Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / AD