      "title": "Plumber",
      "description": "Plumber - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Plumber Martin, TN, United States Job Description Building Services at The University of Tennessee at Martin is currently accepting applications for a Plumber I.  Responsibilities include but are not limited to working on commercial and residential plumbing repairs, maintenance and new installation of the campus plumbing systems. Responding to emergency call backs nights, weekends, and holidays. Responsibilities Perform skilled plumbing work in the completion of assigned daily work orders for maintenance and repairs of domestic plumbing systems by diagnosing the problem and making the proper repairs in academic buildings, dorm rooms and apartments. Which includes unclogging main sewer drain lines, toilets, sinks, tub, and shower units. Installation and repairs of sink & faucets, lavatories & faucets, tub/showers & faucets, toilets & flush valves, urinals & flush valves. Installation of plumbing systems in buildings and remodel work, installing drain lines, vent lines, water lines, gas lines, air lines, vacuum lines, water heaters, boilers, setting faucets and fixtures inside the building. The installation of underground main water and sewer lines. The ability to install water lines and gas piping by measuring, cutting, soldering, using propress tool, pex tool and threading gas pipe. The ability to work with outside contractors on the building projects, fire system inspections & repairs, backflow valve inspections & repairs, boiler inspections & repairs, fiberglass tub inspections & repairs, sump pit pumping. Qualifications Typically requires a high school diploma and one year of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Plumbing experience or a state plumbing license Ability to read and interpret blueprints, technical drawings and do material take offs for projects Knowledge of plumbing codes and regulations Use of all power tools associated with the installation and repairs of plumbing systems Ability to communicate effectively and customer service skills High School Diploma or equivalent Valid driver’s license Application Process: Qualified applicants must apply online and attach a cover letter and resume Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate has been selected Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 9247 Job Category Facilities Services Posting Date 07/30/2026, 10:38 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations 105 Moody Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US EEO/AA STATEMENT / NON-DISCRIMINATION STATEMENT The University of Tennessee is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA institution in the provision of its education and employment programs and services. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of, race, color, national origin, religion, sex, pregnancy, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, or covered veteran status. Inquiries and charges of violation of Title VI (race, color, national origin), Title IX (sex), Section 504 (disability), ADA (disability), ADEA (age), sexual orientation, or veteran status should be directed to the (EEO). Requests for accommodation of a disability should be directed to the ADA Coordinator at the EEO office . © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 105 Moody Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. We know that your privacy is very important to you. Working at UT Why Work at UT About UT Compensation at UT Pre-Employment Background Checks I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Plumber - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers loaded Personal Job Assistant Audio Response Off Clear Ask Me Something Attachment"
