    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/9132": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Administrative Specialist Martin, TN, United States Trending Job Description This position coordinates and performs a wide variety of highly confidential administrative support to the Senior Vice Chancellor for Finance & Administration, the Associate Vice Chancellor and Director of Budget, the Assistant Budget Director, the Sponsored Projects Accountant, the General Ledger Accountant, the Coordinator of Environmental Health & Safety, the Campus Safety Officer, and the Special Assistant to the Vice Chancellor for Strategic Initiatives.  This position serves as a primary point of operational and administrative contact for internal and external constituents, often on complex issues and UT System-wide initiatives.  The administrative specialist works closely with direct reports under the leadership of Finance and Administration to accomplish goals, provide decision making data, and completion of special projects and/or events. Responsibilities •    Manage the logistics of the schedule for SVCFA and plan meetings and trainings for F&A. •    Coordinate incoming/outgoing mail and compose correspondence, reports, records, and disseminate information requiring confidentiality and discretion. •    Provide project management for various F&A Office initiatives, including follow-up and assignment completion. •    Prepare and process transactions, including journal entries, personnel actions, budget revisions, requisitions, purchase orders, invoices, and travel. •    Procure and maintain inventories of equipment and office supplies. •    Assists all visitors and responds to general policies and procedures inquiries for UTM employees. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or some college and specialized education with three to four years of office experience; bachelor’s degree with one to two years of office experience. Good interpersonal skills, flexibility to adjust to changes and short deadlines, and ability to handle several jobs simultaneously Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of computer operating systems and Microsoft Office 365, including Excel, Word, Powerpoint, Teams, and Outlook are strongly preferred.  Experience working in a college or university environment is also desirable. Application Process: Interested candidates must apply online and attach a cover letter, resume, and three (3) references. Application Deadline: Applicant review will begin immediately and continue until a candidate has been selected. Salary range for the position is $19.94 to $24.00 per hour (Market Range 08) - Salary commensurate with education. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 9132 Job Category Administrative Posting Date 07/21/2026, 09:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations 554 University Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US EEO/AA STATEMENT / NON-DISCRIMINATION STATEMENT The University of Tennessee is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA institution in the provision of its education and employment programs and services. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of, race, color, national origin, religion, sex, pregnancy, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, or covered veteran status. Inquiries and charges of violation of Title VI (race, color, national origin), Title IX (sex), Section 504 (disability), ADA (disability), ADEA (age), sexual orientation, or veteran status should be directed to the (EEO). Requests for accommodation of a disability should be directed to the ADA Coordinator at the EEO office . © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 554 University Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. We know that your privacy is very important to you. Working at UT Why Work at UT About UT Compensation at UT Pre-Employment Background Checks I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Administrative Specialist - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers loaded Personal Job Assistant Audio Response Off Clear Ask Me Something Attachment"
