    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/6116": {
      "title": "College Academic Advisor, Engineering and Natural Science Department",
      "description": "College Academic Advisor, Engineering and Natural Science Department - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs College Academic Advisor, Engineering and Natural Science Department Martin, TN, United States Job Description Academic advisors serve a caseload of assigned majors to provide guidance toward degree completion. With support from Department Chairs and the Dean, advisors will display a thorough understanding of curriculum procedures and graduation requirements, advocate for students, and work closely with faculty, student success officers, and academic records to improve student outcomes and success at UTM. Advisors are expected to monitor students' progress and provide resources and appropriate academic interventions as needed in support of UT Martin's student retention and success goals. Advisors are responsible for accurate record keeping, proficiency in all softwares and systems used in advising and registration, and participation in retention strategies and campaigns for their assigned caseloads. Responsibilities Academic Advising -Provide specialized major specific guidance, advocacy, and academic advising to students in an assigned caseload to improve retention and graduation outcomes for students, including course selection, registration, program requirements, and academic policies. -Guide students in developing academic plans aligned with their educational and career goals. -Assist students in understanding and navigating university procedures, such as course withdrawals, course repeat policies, probations, and appeals. -Maintain a thorough working knowledge of all curricular elements of assigned areas and serve on any associated committees or work groups as required. Retention and Student Success -Monitor and analyze student progress and engage in campaigns and research to guide students toward appropriate academic interventions. -Utilize proactive and appreciative advising practices to assist students and identify and mitigate potential barriers to success. -Develop and implement strategies to support retention, persistence, and graduation goals in alignment with college and university initiatives. -Maintain regular communication with faculty and staff to coordinate support for students facing academic or personal challenges. -Identify at-risk students using performance data and proactively conducting outreach to provide guidance, intervention, and referrals to campus resources. Programming and Outreach -Develop and deliver workshops, presentations, and information sessions on academic success, study skills, and degree planning -Support new student orientation, recruitment events, and other programs to promote student engagement and success -Serve as a knowledgeable resource for students, parents, faculty, and staff regarding advising services. Records Management and Reporting -Maintain accurate and confidential student advising records in compliance with FERPA and institutional policies -Prepare reports and summaries for the Dean on advising activities, student progress, and retention data -Ensure student information systems are up-to-date and accurate. Professional Development and Other Duties -Participate in college committees, advising councils, or tasks forces as assigned by the Dean -Engage in ongoing training to stay current with best practices in academic advising and retention strategies -Perform other related duties as assigned to support student success. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field and two years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Advanced degree preferred. Working knowledge of the basic principles of academic advising and the capacity to learn all facets of specific degree programs. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Ability to analyze problems and formulate solutions. Ability to provide excellent customer service. Ability to work constructively on a team and to complete work independently. Ability to learn and understand new systems. Application Process: Qualified candidates must apply online and attach a cover letter and resume. Applicant Deadline: Review of applicant will begin immediately and continue until the candidates have been identified. Minimum hiring rate $37,705.02 (Market Range 07) – Salary commensurate with education and experience. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6116 Job Category Student Services Posting Date 12/10/2025, 09:21 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations 203 Hurt Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US EEO/AA STATEMENT / NON-DISCRIMINATION STATEMENT The University of Tennessee is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA institution in the provision of its education and employment programs and services. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of, race, color, national origin, religion, sex, pregnancy, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, or covered veteran status. Inquiries and charges of violation of Title VI (race, color, national origin), Title IX (sex), Section 504 (disability), ADA (disability), ADEA (age), sexual orientation, or veteran status should be directed to the (EEO). Requests for accommodation of a disability should be directed to the ADA Coordinator at the EEO office . © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © MapTiler © OpenStreetMap contributors | © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 203 Hurt Street, Martin, TN, 38238, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. Non discrimination statement The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution The University of Tennessee is an EEO / AA / Title VI / Title IX / Section 504 / ADA / ADEA institution Privacy Notice We know that your privacy is very important to you. We know that your privacy is very important to you. Working at UT Why Work at UT About UT Compensation at UT Pre-Employment Background Checks I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page College Academic Advisor, Engineering and Natural Science Department - University of Tennessee Career Site Careers loaded Personal Job Assistant Audio Response Off Clear Ask Me Something Attachment"
